# Vim / Neovim :: modes, motions, edits, and the marlinos neovim keys (leader = Space)

## Modes and files
i / a / o :: insert before cursor / after / on a new line below (O above)
Esc :: back to normal mode (also clears search highlight)
:w / :q / :wq / :q! :: save / quit / both / quit without saving
:e <file> :: open a file
v / V / Ctrl+v :: select characters / lines / a block
:<n> :: go to line n (or <n>G)
u / Ctrl+r :: undo / redo
. :: repeat the last change

## Moving
h j k l :: left down up right
w / b / e :: next word / back / end of word (W B E: by spaces)
0 / ^ / $ :: line start / first character / line end
gg / G :: top / bottom of the file
f<c> / t<c> :: to / just before a character on the line (; , repeat)
% :: matching bracket
{ / } :: previous / next blank line (paragraph)
Ctrl+d / Ctrl+u :: half a page down / up
* / # :: next / previous occurrence of the word under the cursor
Ctrl+o / Ctrl+i :: back / forward in the jump list

## Editing (operator + motion)
d<motion> / dd :: delete (cut) / a whole line
c<motion> / cc :: change: delete and insert
y<motion> / yy :: copy (yank) / a line
p / P :: paste after / before
ciw / ci" / ci( :: change inside word / quotes / parens (a instead of i: around)
dap / yip :: delete a paragraph / copy inside one
>> / << :: indent / unindent (in visual: > < keep the selection)
x / r<c> :: delete a character / replace it
J :: join the next line
gc<motion> / gcc :: comment / a line
~ :: toggle case

## Search and replace
/<text> / ?<text> :: search down / up; n N next / previous
:%s/<old>/<new>/g :: replace everywhere (add c to confirm each)
:s/<old>/<new>/g :: on this line (or the selection)
:g/<text>/d :: delete every matching line

## Files, buffers, windows (marlinos)
Space Space :: find files
Space / :: grep the project
Space , :: open buffers
Space fr / fw / fh / fk :: recent files / grep word / help / keymaps
Space f. :: resume the last search
- :: file browser of the current directory (oil: edit it like text, :w applies)
Shift+h / Shift+l :: previous / next buffer
Ctrl+h j k l :: move between split windows
:sp / :vsp :: split horizontal / vertical; Ctrl+w q closes one

## Code (LSP)
gd :: go to definition
K :: documentation under the cursor
grn / gra :: rename / code action
grr / gri :: references / implementations
[d / ]d :: previous / next diagnostic; Space cl shows it
Space cf :: format (file or selection)
Space cs / cS :: symbols in the file / the project
Space cd / cD :: diagnostics in the file / the project
Space uh :: toggle inline type hints
Ctrl+s :: (insert) signature help

## Git (gitsigns)
]h / [h :: next / previous changed hunk
Space gs / gr :: stage / reset the hunk
Space gp :: preview the hunk
Space gb :: toggle blame on the line
Space gd :: diff the file
Space gc / gS :: commits / status (fzf)

## Macros and registers
q<r> … q :: record a macro into register r
@<r> / @@ :: play it / again (5@r: five times)
"<r>y / "<r>p :: yank into / paste from a register
"+y / "+p :: system clipboard
:reg :: show registers
> press Space and wait: which-key lists every marlinos mapping
